    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for a derived `riskFlag` on the owner read model that is `true` when **any** of three signals holds \u2014 possible duplicate, disposable-adjacent email domain, or city over its soft capacity \u2014 and `false` otherwise.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `riskFlag` read-only boolean property to the `Owner` schema (the generator source for `OwnerDto`), documenting the three-way OR rule.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/RiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 a null-safe derivation helper following the existing mapper-helper pattern (`Locality`, `Membership`, etc.). It OR-combines:\n   - `possibleDuplicate` \u2014 the existing soft-duplicate flag set at creation by `CheckPossibleDuplicate`.\n   - `capacityWarning` \u2014 the existing \"city over its soft capacity\" flag set at read time by `MarkCityCapacityWarning` (true once the city reaches the soft warn threshold of 40, below the hard cap of 50).\n   - **disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 a new, softer neighbourhood check around the existing hard blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`): a domain is adjacent when one of its labels is a known disposable base name, catching a different TLD (`mailinator.net`) or a subdomain (`inbox.mailinator.com`). Exact blocklisted domains are already rejected with 400 at creation, so this covers only what gets through.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `riskFlag` via `@Mapping(... expression = \"...RiskFlag.of(owner)\")`, matching how every other derived field is mapped.\n\nNote on interpretation: the task supplied only the one-sentence spec, and \"disposable-adjacent\" wasn't defined elsewhere in the codebase (no test pins its exact behaviour beyond the false-normally case in `Cp58Tests`). I anchored it to the existing disposable blocklist as the most defensible reading. The full suite (70 tests) is green.",
